    {
      "id": "0vDa8PAh5gNdLGEU-GNBb",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -9494.375357341072,
      "y": 20498.43439240342,
      "width": 1574.4291076660156,
      "height": 490,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "dashed",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "c0HQ",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1491417945,
      "version": 1027,
      "versionNonce": 1123501751,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1784790718808,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Broker:  the servers (logical or physical ) that holds the \"queues\"\n\nPartitions: the queue, an ordered immutable sequence of messages that we append to, like a log file. Each broker can have\nmultiple partitions\n\n\nTopic : Logical group of data (partitions ) where you consume from or publish to . Partition is the actual data containers and\ntopics are logical grouping. broker is server which contains these logical set called topic which further contains the actual\nordered partition which is nothing but queue\n\nProducer : produces or writes to the topic (kafka) \n\nConsumer: consumes or reads from topic or partition or queue from kafka\n    ",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Broker:  the servers (logical or physical ) that holds the \"queues\"\n\nPartitions: the queue, an ordered immutable sequence of messages that we append to, like a log file. Each broker can have multiple partitions\n\n\nTopic : Logical group of data (partitions ) where you consume from or publish to . Partition is the actual data containers and topics are logical grouping. broker is server which contains these logical set called topic which further contains the actual ordered partition which is nothing but queue\n\nProducer : produces or writes to the topic (kafka) \n\nConsumer: consumes or reads from topic or partition or queue from kafka\n    ",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
