      "seed": 1956839673,
      "version": 64,
      "versionNonce": 177950361,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1784790718808,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Each partition in Kafka functions essentially as an append-only log file. \nMessages are sequentially added to the end of this log, which is why Kafka is commonly described as a distributed commit log. \nThis append-only design is central to Kafka’s architecture, providing several important benefits",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Each partition in Kafka functions essentially as an append-only log file. \nMessages are sequentially added to the end of this log, which is why Kafka is commonly described as a distributed commit log. \nThis append-only design is central to Kafka’s architecture, providing several important benefits",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "MeiWvaSnSsJ8QrvUkRGvH",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -8535.07327400774,
      "y": 23646.54897573675,
      "width": 1683.2467041015625,
      "height": 140,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "c0I8",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2120907225,
      "version": 95,
      "versionNonce": 2054767479,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1784790718808,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. Immutability: Once written, messages in a partition cannot be altered in-place. \nThey are eventually removed through retention policies or log compaction, but they're never modified. \nThis immutability is crucial for Kafka's performance and reliability. \nIt simplifies replication, speeds up recovery processes, and avoids consistency issues common in systems where data can be changed.",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. Immutability: Once written, messages in a partition cannot be altered in-place. \nThey are eventually removed through retention policies or log compaction, but they're never modified. \nThis immutability is crucial for Kafka's performance and reliability. \nIt simplifies replication, speeds up recovery processes, and avoids consistency issues common in systems where data can be changed.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "ICuvUOqPTb6tMq3TFMrqx",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -8537.62014900774,
      "y": 23838.10366323675,
      "width": 1108.0992431640625,
      "height": 70,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "c0I9",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1452267193,
      "version": 10,
      "versionNonce": 2001212281,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1784790718808,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "2. Efficiency: By restricting operations to appending data at the end of the log, \nKafka minimizes disk seek times, which are a major bottleneck in many storage systems.",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "2. Efficiency: By restricting operations to appending data at the end of the log, \nKafka minimizes disk seek times, which are a major bottleneck in many storage systems.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "JV85y1cXduyCNB9TJRycl",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -8541.62014900774,
      "y": 23946.10366323675,
      "width": 1258.2630615234375,
      "height": 105,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "c0IA",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1068930969,
      "version": 15,
      "versionNonce": 261078167,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1784790718808,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "3. Scalability: The simplicity of the append-only log mechanism facilitates horizontal scaling. \nMore partitions can be added and distributed across a cluster of brokers to handle increasing loads, \nand each partition can be replicated across multiple brokers to enhance fault tolerance.",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "3. Scalability: The simplicity of the append-only log mechanism facilitates horizontal scaling. \nMore partitions can be added and distributed across a cluster of brokers to handle increasing loads, \nand each partition can be replicated across multiple brokers to enhance fault tolerance.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
